        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "63a9c1e9-eb7d-5580-b265-f1ce978c38ed",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Treaty of Springwells, War of 1812\n- Peoples: Odawa, Wyandot, Delaware, Seneca, Shawnee, Miami, Chippewa, Ottawa, Potawatomi\n- Countries: United States, Canada\n\nFacts:\n- The Treaty of Springwells was an agreement between the United States and the Wyandot, Delaware, Seneca, Shawnee, Miami, Chippewa, Ottawa, and Potawatomi Indians.\n- The Treaty of Springwells ended the conflict between the United States and those Indigenous groups that was part of the War of 1812.\n- The Odawa, also called Ottawa or Odaawaa, are an Indigenous American ethnic group.\n- The name Odawa is said to mean \"traders.\"\n- The Odawa primarily inhabit land in the northern United States and southern Canada.",
